      "content": "The sudden influx of immigrants like South Asians into a historically white working-class suburb often leads to friction because of cultural differences and perceived changes to the neighborhood's established norms. These shifts can create social tension as long-term residents feel their way of life is being diluted or threatened. This demographic change can lead to cultural clashes over local customs, businesses, and community identity.",
