      "content": "Researchers often point to changes in local retail, such as the replacement of established businesses with ethnic grocery stores, as a visible sign of change. Social indicators might include increased community complaints regarding noise or differing religious practices becoming more visible in public spaces. Economically, shifts in housing demand and property values can create resentment among existing residents who feel priced out or marginalized by the new demographic. These visible changes are often interpreted by some as a decline in the neighborhood's original character.",
