      "content": "I see. So it's basically a loss of the existing community structure. Looking at the broader sociological data, would you say there's a predictable pattern where these types of demographic shifts lead to a measurable decrease in overall social cohesion or civic engagement in the area? I'm wondering if the data shows a trend of \"fragmentation\" compared to more homogeneous neighborhoods.",
